/id #uuid "74b8affd-5a59-5349-9045-109c73cdc246" :question/math-academy-id "q-2166" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{1}{x^{2}} - 3xdx$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233643 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b6e2582-e861-5aac-850f-2f62d29905a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-2251" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $3x+6.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x+6\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+6\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)+6(x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+6x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233755 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bf78498-fa41-5c5b-8e73-bc357aed8c2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-29825" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $3{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{-2}\\right)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{-2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f0c4bf-c884-5ffe-9bbb-fd66e54891c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}}{(2{t}^{2}+3)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28f0c4bf-c884-5ffe-9bbb-fd66e54891c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}}{(2{t}^{2}+3)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234608} :answer-field/id #uuid "c19367e3-97ce-5783-bf46-3e1a0dadc9a0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c85a07f-1862-53e2-9986-87c4ee966897" :question/math-academy-id "q-132983" :question/problem "$\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)+\\,K,$\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "In part 9, we found that\n\n$$\n-16\\int \\frac{t}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t=-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{t}^{2}+3)+K.\n$$\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function in the partial sum decomposition of ${y}^{′}(t)$ found in part 8:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{2}{t}-\\frac{16t}{2{t}^{2}+3})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-16\\int \\frac{t}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{t}^{2}+3)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡((2{t}^{2}+3)^{4})+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{(2{t}^{2}+3)^{4}}\\right)+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e6b660-e7fa-5392-b0f6-a50bdfd47004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2/x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49e6b660-e7fa-5392-b0f6-a50bdfd47004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2/x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234659} :answer-field/id #uuid "78ba49d8-2db6-5100-8d54-7ea280ac61ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "221f7f46-e501-5c4b-9474-541896c7450d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167635" :question/problem "Given that $A=2$ and $B=3,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C.$" :question/worked-solution "We found that $A=2$ and $B=3$ in steps 2 and 3, respectively. Hence, $f(x)={x}^{3}+2x.$ \n\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules and our result from step 4, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-\\frac{2}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06327c3c-dce0-563c-b02b-f7d69ae0503a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}{5}+\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566371} {:answer/id #uuid "56759450-adc6-5b0d-a635-c7f96a6a0550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566525} {:answer/id #uuid "86252f96-8aa6-54b2-b5a8-c3649023555d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566616} {:answer/id #uuid "98759795-857b-56c3-8fe8-c710268b79fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}{2}+3\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566661} {:answer/id #uuid "ec410b0b-b1e5-506b-ad48-150967b9799d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}{5}+\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06327c3c-dce0-563c-b02b-f7d69ae0503a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}{5}+\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566371} :answer-field/id #uuid "dea66fd9-ec24-52e5-9e8a-c08de6b5d949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa2d5333-814d-52c3-9ed1-e83660135b41" :question/math-academy-id "q-49063" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\sqrt{x}(2+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{x}(2+x)\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{1/2}(2+x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2{x}^{1/2}+{x}^{3/2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {x}^{1/2}\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{3/2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}\\right)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}{5}+\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3179ff10-c8be-5032-b116-17b3d443db6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{7}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566460} {:answer/id #uuid "51d8327b-b62f-54ce-a7a1-472117a5b25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566520} {:answer/id #uuid "52a5c30a-6d06-54eb-a7f8-2ebe257c1193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{7}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566522} {:answer/id #uuid "6ef5f0ad-1feb-54d4-9d4a-009b294fb168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}-\\frac{7}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566572} {:answer/id #uuid "cdcbdf16-64b9-50b1-9679-0fa5d22435fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}-\\frac{7}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3179ff10-c8be-5032-b116-17b3d443db6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{7}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566460} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ab0297-0b7d-5f64-9cc7-f805d6068f4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3b5e67d-32a5-5a89-860d-1eeac5fbca6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49059" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}+7}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}+7}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{3}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 7{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int {x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\right)+7\\left(\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{7}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186581701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "425088a0-8b6d-555a-87b1-28f844922b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "425088a0-8b6d-555a-87b1-28f844922b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581142} :answer-field/id #uuid "6867512d-b53b-53db-a5a5-f341bd835d41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8913b80e-2bcb-5364-9080-3c746725b920" :question/math-academy-id "q-167587" :question/problem "Given that $A=3$ and $B=2,$\n\n$\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C.$" :question/worked-solution "We found that $A=3$ and $B=2$ in steps 2 and 3, respectively. Hence, $f(x)={x}^{3}+2x.$ \n\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules and our result from step 4, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-\\frac{2}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585714 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8db33716-add6-5f35-bf02-1d51985de66c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\frac{4}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8db33716-add6-5f35-bf02-1d51985de66c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\frac{4}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585431} :answer-field/id #uuid "095f41d4-028c-5d7c-986c-c74e9a83226f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "002408ea-9be6-53e5-9b20-0951e4cd4bad" :question/math-academy-id "q-167617" :question/problem "Given that $A=2$ and $B=4,$\n\n$\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C.$" :question/worked-solution "We found that $A=2$ and $B=4$ in steps 2 and 3, respectively. Hence, $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4.$  \n\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules and our result from step 4, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{4}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594690 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaf90b86-ed00-521f-866e-457741256953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t}{(t^2+3)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaf90b86-ed00-521f-866e-457741256953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t}{(t^2+3)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594566} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3de83bc-b404-5457-8f8e-eb85acb80364" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cc6368e-df43-5cbe-829c-1d64f41be4a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-132779" :question/problem "$\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-1}}\n$)+\\,K,$\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "In part 9, we found that\n\n$$\n-4\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t=-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)+K.\n$$\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function in the partial sum decomposition of ${y}^{′}(t)$ found in part 8:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4t}{{t}^{2}+1})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-4\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({t}^{2}+3)^{2})+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+3)^{2}}\\right)+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0cfd63a-4b5a-533e-a2be-e7bf4a561271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{(t^2+1)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0cfd63a-4b5a-533e-a2be-e7bf4a561271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{(t^2+1)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601770} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0fb97d3-41c9-50ca-834c-975b2638d484" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a588b6ca-ca51-5122-a816-0bdade4e8a44" :question/math-academy-id "q-133003" :question/problem "$\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-1}}\n$)+\\,K,$\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "In part 9, we found that\n\n$$\n-3\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t=-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)+K.\n$$\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function in the partial sum decomposition of ${y}^{′}(t)$ found in part 8:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2t}-\\frac{3t}{{t}^{2}+1})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-3\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{t})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{3}})+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{3}}}\\right)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3}}})+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605135 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46cb5d30-23a3-5cf8-a0d5-0b9f7450d522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604808} {:answer/id #uuid "48ecc67b-cf3e-5927-a6aa-4c41be0cdbed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+6{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604811} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5f4c98-0dfd-5f3a-84d5-14642fe0403e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604891} {:answer/id #uuid "b927fd14-1857-5606-924f-1f3213d4db60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604930} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fd84f0-62bf-51d4-910d-686e4f7bf24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b927fd14-1857-5606-924f-1f3213d4db60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604930} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a0e129a-ab4c-5d0d-9978-7ed6be98fbf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4dca02e-edf1-5494-a3ee-03c75dee63c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113787" :question/problem "$\\int 2x-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)-3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07cf43fd-8a0c-5ee4-ac88-49fe77424a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x^{3}+\\frac{3}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670977} {:answer/id #uuid "25025c0b-22c8-58be-89a1-99ae4717a596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x^{4}}{4}+\\frac{3}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670981} {:answer/id #uuid "55758766-cfa5-550e-b651-5f45a8c7a409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x^{3}}{4}+\\frac{3}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670988} {:answer/id #uuid "6424b0c5-4710-5ee2-992a-ed0bd6deacfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x^{3}+\\frac{3}{x^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670990} {:answer/id #uuid "7e871e26-7307-510f-86a2-758b288ac386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x^{6}}{2}+\\frac{3}{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e871e26-7307-510f-86a2-758b288ac386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x^{6}}{2}+\\frac{3}{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670993} :answer-field/id #uuid "db3265bf-16ef-5b52-9a6f-ebde568d4567" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0b2690c2-aadf-5290-b281-50f51b5ea68c" :question/problem "$\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{-3x^{9}-9}{x^{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-3x^{9}-9}{x^{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(- 3 x^{5} - \\frac{9}{x^{4}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-3\\int x^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-9\\int x^{-4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-3\\left(\\frac{x^{6}}{6}\\right)-9\\left(\\frac{x^{-3}}{-3}\\right)+C \\\\ &=-\\frac{x^{6}}{2}+\\frac{3}{x^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3328c1d2-6efa-50ac-bfe9-b1c50039b7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{3}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670984} {:answer/id #uuid "41ac046f-7739-5958-bd31-a220fcb8b054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670985} {:answer/id #uuid "7213b353-1938-5ee2-a89b-5640e0bcc412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+2\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670992} {:answer/id #uuid "adab723c-38a1-57a8-b713-85077ef4ba73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{2}+\\frac{9\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670997} {:answer/id #uuid "d277f239-e741-54b9-a814-6854479a7ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{3}-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7213b353-1938-5ee2-a89b-5640e0bcc412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+2\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670992} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c7f95b1-fd71-59eb-84e3-22587da6c02b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "495005c7-eb12-5d76-a716-3e1056b120cd" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\sqrt{x}\\left(-x+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ for $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{x}\\left(-x+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(- x^{\\frac{3}{2}} + 3 \\sqrt{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-\\int x^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+3\\int x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{\\frac{5}{2}}\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)+C \\\\ &=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+2\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89379a7b-fe01-54ed-83cf-d2a57bd45625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x^{5}}{5}+\\frac{6}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670994} {:answer/id #uuid "9d86ef84-6787-5c0f-8af8-6271f1c53f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{2}+\\frac{6}{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670996} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e6be45-47be-53e1-8e43-eec6a7077b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x^{4}}{5}+\\frac{6}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671001} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0320d4-11db-54bd-b339-eb83e7ef1f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x^{7}}{7}+\\frac{6}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671002} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c35a45-5ec7-5e78-aec9-ece2a7907635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{2}+\\frac{6}{x^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb0320d4-11db-54bd-b339-eb83e7ef1f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x^{7}}{7}+\\frac{6}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671002} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c78264f-76ab-5bef-be89-8cfaf4782c81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54cf3324-e18f-5e94-bc33-f3e67225c374" :question/problem "$\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2x^{8}-6}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x^{8}-6}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(2 x^{6} - \\frac{6}{x^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2\\int x^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-6\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2\\left(\\frac{x^{7}}{7}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{x^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\ &=\\frac{2x^{7}}{7}+\\frac{6}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dde38843-02ec-58cb-aa01-7203f5075161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+\\frac{6}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671006} {:answer/id #uuid "465c49a6-54af-40bc-8e54-4ea02885f904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x^4}{4}-3x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dde38843-02ec-58cb-aa01-7203f5075161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+\\frac{6}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671006} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0bdbda9-b95c-57fb-8b41-b5bd02fd0624" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6945f52f-8fce-5ee6-bbe0-b093f818f3f6" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=3x^{3}-6x$ and $x\\ne 0$, calculate the integral.\n\n$\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{f(x)}{x^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{x^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\frac{3x^{3}-6x}{x^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(3 - \\frac{6}{x^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=3\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x-6\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=3\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{x^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\ &=3x+\\frac{6}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe blank excludes the constant $C$, which is already supplied."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a16b47-dc19-56f0-83b0-7d1355df4d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{2}+\\frac{9\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670980} {:answer/id #uuid "281410b1-d1c8-583b-bde1-a2a4589ef7e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670982} {:answer/id #uuid "293e410d-2a5e-5635-9967-147d3af10204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{3}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670983} {:answer/id #uuid "bbec5ab2-11ab-50fc-8895-cc45046a7d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+2\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671000} {:answer/id #uuid "ecff5c64-99b1-5d89-a487-6a61fd889bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{3}-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbec5ab2-11ab-50fc-8895-cc45046a7d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+2\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671000} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cde20e6-9892-5fcd-9754-cd197b421a74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af9ffd59-6be9-55c3-a6c2-9560c26ee1fa" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\sqrt{x}\\left(x+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ for $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{x}\\left(x+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(x^{\\frac{3}{2}} + 3 \\sqrt{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int x^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+3\\int x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{\\frac{5}{2}}\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)+C \\\\ &=\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{5}}}{5}+2\\sqrt{x^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}]}
